[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:82. Monster or Fish]
[00:00.780]Passage 82 | 文章八十二
[00:02.510]Monster or Fish? | 怪物还是鱼？
[00:05.610]Fishermen and sailors sometimes claimed to have seen monsters in the sea. | 渔民和水手有时声称在海上见过怪物。
[00:12.270]Though people have often laughed at stories told by seamen, | 尽管人们常常嘲笑水手讲述的故事，
[00:16.725]it is now known that many of these monsters, | 但现在已知，许多这些怪物，
[00:20.500]which have at times been sighted, | 有时曾被目击过，
[00:22.705]are simply strange fish. | 它们只是奇怪的鱼。
[00:25.515]Occasionally, unusual creatures are washed to the shore, | 偶尔，不寻常的生物会被冲到岸边，
[00:30.490]but they are rarely caught out at sea. | 但它们很少在海上被捕获。
[00:34.005]Sometime ago, however, a peculiar fish was caught near Madagascar. | 然而，不久前，在马达加斯加附近捕获了一条奇特的鱼。
[00:40.895]A small fishing boat was carried miles out to sea | 一艘小型渔船被拖离海岸数英里，
[00:45.545]by the powerful fish as it pulled on the line. | 因为这条强壮的鱼在拉扯鱼线。
[00:49.360]Realizing that this was no ordinary fish, | 意识到这不是一条普通的鱼，
[00:53.185]the fishermen made every effort not to damage it in any way. | 渔民们竭尽全力不以任何方式损坏它。
[00:58.365]When it was eventually brought to shore, | 当它最终被带上岸时，
[01:01.960]it was found to be over 13 feet long. | 发现它有13英尺多长。
[01:05.930]It had a head like a horse, | 它有一个像马一样的头，
[01:08.730]big blue eyes, shining silver skin, | 大大的蓝眼睛，闪亮的银色皮肤，
[01:12.770]and a bright red tail. | 和一条鲜红的尾巴。
[01:15.505]The fish, which has since been sent to a museum, | 这条鱼后来被送往博物馆，
[01:19.420]where it is being examined by a scientist, | 正在由科学家进行检查，
[01:22.240]is called an oar fish. | 它被称为皇带鱼。
[01:24.675]Such creatures have rarely been seen alive by man, | 这种生物很少被人活着看到，
[01:28.875]as they live at a depth of 600 feet. | 因为它们生活在600英尺深的海底。